        "purpose": "transcribing",
        "value": "一小隊ニ付役人六人步兵四十人"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "modern_jp_reading",
        "value": "一小隊に付き、役人六人・歩兵四十人（いちしょうたいにつき やくにん ろくにん・ほへい よんじゅうにん）"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "english_translation",
        "value": "Two-register warichu qualifying the platoon count: per platoon, six officers and forty infantrymen. The right sub-column holds the label 一小隊ニ付 (five glyphs, ending at y1902); the left sub-column holds 役人六人 and then, after a one-glyph gap, 步兵四十人. Eight platoons at forty-six men come to 368, but no total is printed for Utsunomiya on this leaf - its artillery and drummers run on to the right of the Ushiku maru-marker on lower_p198_left, so the establishment cannot be summed from this page alone."
      },
      {
        "purpose": "identifying",
        "value": "宇都宮步兵割書"
      }
    ],
